WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:03.600
There are many people who
misunderstand what fiction is.

00:00:03.600 --> 00:00:06.540
They'll say, "Fiction
is a bunch of lies."

00:00:06.540 --> 00:00:09.420
I would say fiction is
actually one of the best

00:00:09.420 --> 00:00:12.150
ways for finding truth.

00:00:12.150 --> 00:00:14.070
When I started writing
"The Joy Luck Club,"

00:00:14.070 --> 00:00:15.600
I was such a novice.

00:00:15.600 --> 00:00:21.050
There was so much I
didn't know about writing.

00:00:21.050 --> 00:00:24.500
As you ask yourself,
"What do I have

00:00:24.500 --> 00:00:26.780
in my life to write about?"--

00:00:26.780 --> 00:00:28.460
Believe me, you have plenty.

00:00:31.230 --> 00:00:33.450
In this class, I'm
going to give you

00:00:33.450 --> 00:00:36.990
guideposts-- examples of
things that worked and also

00:00:36.990 --> 00:00:37.960
didn't work.

00:00:37.960 --> 00:00:40.740
I'm going to show you
rejection letters.

00:00:40.740 --> 00:00:43.290
I'm going to show you
the tools you already

00:00:43.290 --> 00:00:46.390
have at your disposal,
which is your own thoughts,

00:00:46.390 --> 00:00:49.680
your own memory, and your
own form of imagination.

00:00:49.680 --> 00:00:54.600
You can use your past as
the tool of your trade;

00:00:54.600 --> 00:00:58.810
and me, the writer, is
saying, "This is good."

00:00:58.810 --> 00:01:00.480
It's bad when it happened.

00:01:00.480 --> 00:01:03.300
Me, the writer-- "This is
good," because what I can do

00:01:03.300 --> 00:01:09.820
now is take that visceral
sensation, and I can use it.

00:01:09.820 --> 00:01:13.330
"My father has asked me to be
the fourth corner at the Joy

00:01:13.330 --> 00:01:14.230
Luck Club.

00:01:14.230 --> 00:01:18.190
I am to replace my mother,
whose seat at the mahjong table

00:01:18.190 --> 00:01:21.550
has been empty since
she died two months ago.

00:01:21.550 --> 00:01:26.630
My father thinks she was
killed by her own thoughts."

00:01:26.630 --> 00:01:31.650
Imbalance, crisis--
that moves you forward.

00:01:31.650 --> 00:01:34.790
You don't have to have
trauma to be a writer.

00:01:34.790 --> 00:01:38.440
What you need to
have is perspective.

00:01:38.440 --> 00:01:41.510
If you have a seriousness
of purpose, which

00:01:41.510 --> 00:01:46.190
is to understand yourself,
human nature, the world,

00:01:46.190 --> 00:01:50.690
and the conflicts that make
us infinitely interesting,

00:01:50.690 --> 00:01:55.570
you will find the stories
that you want to tell.

00:01:55.570 --> 00:02:00.510
I'm Amy Tan, and this
is my MasterClass.

